Dear Henrik,

I am testing 10 of our Affymetrix 500K samples using aroma.affymetrix
v1.0.0. I followed the steps described in "Estimation of total copy
numbers using the CRMA v2 method". However, in the step of calibration
for crosstalk between allele probe pairs (acc <-
AllelicCrosstalkCalibration(csR, model="CRMAv2")), I noticed that in
your example three tags would be added after this process "ACC,ra,-
XY", while in my case, only "ACC,-XY" were added. I also tried
different models, including the default one "asis", and "CRMA", still
two tags ("ACC,-XY") were added. So what does the tag "ra" mean? are
there different tags corresponding to different models used? If not,
how can different models be differentiated after the calibration?

Thanks!

Harry

